code and point Zumi\u2019s camera at your face. Note that it might take some time for Zumi to take and display an image.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22150792571\" name=\"6a22150792571\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Review<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">With this lesson, you have learned how to detect faces in images using Zumi\u2019s camera! Face detection can be used for a variety of things, such as alerting Zumi to when a person is in front of her or running a piece of code when a face is detected. Try combining the find face block with other functions and see what programs you can come up with!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;2938&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 4 Taking an Image [vc_column_text]Similar to detecting QR codes or signs, in order to detect a face you must take a picture using Zumi\u2019s camera functions. Drag the&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/face-detection\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":2897,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":2878,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[2108,3202,2122,2126,2230],"class_list":["post-3438","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-face-detection","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-senior","lesson-tag-zumi","module-senior","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3438","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"colle